ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 25862, Dec. 16, 2014>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Decree shall enter into force on December 19, 2014.
Article 2 (Preparation regarding imposition, of charges)
(1) In order to advance with projects for relief of injury smoothly, the head of the Institute of Drug Safety and Risk Management to whom the duties of imposition and collection of charges are entrusted pursuant to the latter part of Article 86-2(1) of the Act, may determine the rate for imposing charges for basic charges to be imposed in 2015, after approval by the Minister of Food and Drug Safety, before this Decree enters into force pursuant to subparagraph 1d of the Appendix; provided, deliberation by the Finance Steering Committee may be omitted.
(2) Before this Decree enters into force, the head of the Institute of Drug Safety and Risk Management to whom the duties of imposition and collection of charges are entrusted pursuant to the latter part of Article 86-2(1) of the Act, may pre-notify a drug manufacturer, of the details of the amount and calculation of basic charges calculated in accordance with subparagraph 1 of the Appendix, for which the rate for imposing charges referred to in paragraph (1) is applied, and allow them to peruse such details.
(3) Where the head of the Institute of Drug Safety and Risk Management deems that the operation of the Finance Steering Committee is necessary, he or she may constitute the Finance Steering Committee pursuant to Article 14 before this Decree enters into force.
Article 3 (Scope of incremental payment of allowances for recovering from injuries)
Benefits for relief of injury shall be paid incrementally, according to the following classifications, pursuant to Article 4 of the Addenda to the partially amended Pharmaceutical Affairs Act (Act No. 12450):
1. By December 31, 2015: payment of lump-sum compensation for death;
2. From January 1, 2016 to December 31, 2016: payment of lump-sum compensation for death, funeral expenses, and lump-sum compensation for disability;
3. After January 1, 2017: payment of benefits for relief of injury under any of subparagraphs of Article 86-3(1) of the Act.
Article 4 Omitted.

